  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 177,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Breast mass: BENIGN or MALIGNANT?",
   "lines": [
    "1 · STABLE? check for cancer EMERGENCIES first: cord compression, superior vena cava obstruction, hypercalcemia, febrile neutropenia",
    "2 · History + exam: where (clock face, depth), size, edge, consistency, mobility · nipple, skin, nodes, the other breast",
    "3 · Image: ULTRASOUND first for a palpable lump, pain, discharge or age < 30 · then diagnostic mammogram",
    "older = more likely cancer · NO blood or urine test identifies a breast mass"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_b",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 192,
   "w": 744,
   "h": 96,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "BENIGN feel",
   "lines": [
    "SMOOTH edge · MOBILE · soft or firm · CHANGES with periods · may be tender"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_m",
